{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Unto the woman He said, etc.</b> HaShem intended to state three curses corresponding to the three things stated in the matter: ״כִּי טוֹב הָעֵץ״ (Genesis 3:6), etc., and ״כִּי תַאֲוָה״ (Genesis 3:6), etc., and ״וְנֶחְמָד״ (Genesis 3:6), etc. Corresponding to ״כִּי טוֹב הָעֵץ״ — that she desired to indulge and to find pleasure contrary to the will of the Blessed One — He multiplied her sorrow, even at a time of joy: ״בְּעֶצֶב תֵּלְדִי בָנִים.״ And corresponding to ״וְכִי תַאֲוָה״ etc., He said ״וְאֶל אִישֵׁךְ תְּשׁוּקָתֵךְ״ — that she will always desire him, and in this there are two particulars of curse: the first is that she will desire and it will not be in her power to fulfill her desire, but rather in the hand of the husband, and this particular is included in the general statement of ״וְהוּא יִמְשָׁל בָּךְ.״ The second is that she will not have the means to fulfill her craving, and you will find that in this particular the woman differs from the man, for the man is satiated in his craving whereas the woman is not — understand this; and this is a great curse, that she is always lacking fulfillment of her craving. And this corresponds to the trait of desire of the eyes. And corresponding to ״נֶחְמָד״ etc., He said ״וְהוּא יִמְשָׁל״ etc.: she thought to remove from herself the power of the great ruler, to be like Elohim, etc.; He added to her a ruler to subdue her."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:38:54.648048657Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}